From: Nerves system for the SMT1019
Subject: [PATCH] dts: rk3576 wf1019: cap WiFi SDIO bus at 50 MHz high-speed

At the dts-requested 200 MHz SDR104 the WiFi SDIO link is unstable on this
hardware: tuning fails ("dwmmc_rockchip 2a320000.mmc: All phases bad!",
"mmc2: tuning execution failed: -5") and the bus collapses after a short
period of traffic (bcmsdh_sdmmc write errors -110/-84/-5, endless
"dhdsdio_htclk: HT Avail timeout"), killing wpa_supplicant/DHCP mid-flight.

Cap the bus at 50 MHz high-speed mode, which involves no tuning. Plenty of
bandwidth for the AP6281S radio; stability over throughput during bring-up.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3576s-r157-v2.0-wf1019-linux.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3576s-r157-v2.0-wf1019-linux.dts
@@ -745,7 +745,7 @@
 };

 &sdio {
-	max-frequency = <200000000>;
+	max-frequency = <50000000>;
 	no-sd;
 	no-mmc;
 	bus-width = <4>;
@@ -757,7 +757,6 @@
 	non-removable;
 	pinctrl-names = "default";
 	pinctrl-0 = <&sdmmc1m0_bus4 &sdmmc1m0_clk &sdmmc1m0_cmd>;
-	sd-uhs-sdr104;
 	vcc-supply = <&wifi_pwr>;
 	status = "okay";
 };
